bcachefs-tools-1.39.7: guard inode_state_* helpers for kernel 6.18.64

kernel 6.18.64 backported the inode_state_* accessors into
include/linux/fs.h, so the 6.19.0 version guard is wrong: both
definitions get compiled and the helpers collide as redefinitions.

    src/fs/bcachefs/vfs/fs.h:17:24: error: redefinition of 'inode_state_read'

Bump the guard to 6.18.64 so the built-in versions are skipped and
the kernel's own definitions (include/linux/fs.h) are used.
--- a/fs/vfs/fs.h
+++ b/fs/vfs/fs.h
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/stat.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>

-#if !defined(__KERNEL__) || LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,19,0)
+#if !defined(__KERNEL__) || LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,18,64)
 static inline unsigned inode_state_read(struct inode *inode)
 {
 	return inode->i_state;
